              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to United States, respondent Alphonso Vonn pleaded guilty with counsel present after being advised of his right to assistance of counsel at all stages of the proceedings."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Defendant",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5d7b37896171-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 51,
              "start": 51
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Defendant, the defendant denied that he personally possessed a gun or had knowledge of co\u2011defendants possessing guns."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5d7b37896171-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5d7b37896171-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The central legal question is whether the failure to advise the right to assistance of counsel during the plea colloquy constitutes a reversible error subject to harmless error review or plain error review."
      }
    ],
